IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`
IMPORT `kn-majority`

-- Mishnah Kinnim, CHAPTER 3: the priest who did not ask, and what the owner must bring again.
-- Target compiler: main.  Counts are of BIRDS unless a name says pairs.
-- Chapter 1's count (kn-ch1.l4) is what may be offered before the fact; this chapter's is how many
-- offerings were certainly valid after it (Reiss section 4 calls these the second and third senses of
-- "valid"): the fewest over every way the priest could have shared the birds out.
-- GENERATED from tools/kn-ch3.l4.in by tools/render.py; edit the template.

§ `Kinnim chapter 3`

§§ `3:1 and 3:2 nests mixed, offered by a priest who did not ask`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:2 | במה דברים אמורים, בכהן נמלך.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:3 | אבל בכהן שאינו נמלך, אחת לזו ואחת לזו, שתים לזו ושתים לזו, שלש לזו ושלש לזו:
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:4 | [ עשה ] כולן למעלה, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:5 | כולן למטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:6 | חצים למעלה וחצים למטה: את שלמעלה, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול, ואת שלמטה, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- When is this said?  Of a priest who asks.  But of a priest who does not ask: one to this woman and
-- one to that, two and two, three and three: he made them all above: half valid and half invalid; all
-- below: half valid and half invalid; half above and half below: of those above, half valid and half
-- invalid, and of those below, half valid and half invalid.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:8 | אחת לזו ושתים לזו, ושלש לזו, ועשר לזו, ומאה לזו:
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:9 | עשה כולן למעלה, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:10 | כולן למטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:11 | חצין למעלן וחצין למטן, המרובה כשר.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:12 | זה הכלל, כל מקום שאתה יכול לחלוק את הקנין ולא יהו משל אשה אחת, בין מלמעלן בין מלמטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13 | כל מקום שאין אתה יכול לחלוק את הקנין עד שיהו משל אשה אחת, בין מלמעלן בין מלמטן, המרובה כשר.
-- One to this and two to that, and three to that, and ten to that, and a hundred to that: he made them
-- all above: half valid and half invalid; all below: half valid and half invalid; half above and half
-- below: the majority is valid.  This is the general principle (quoted at kn-majority.l4).
--
-- The answer, in birds, is the fewest valid offerings.  All above: the burnt offerings, half the birds;
-- all below: the sin offerings, half the birds.  Half above and half below: half, where the general
-- principle's first clause holds; otherwise the majority, read with Koppel and Reiss (other readings:
-- kn-majority.l4).  Any other split is not in the text, and answers NOTHING (fork F5; the worst-case
-- principle beyond the text is a separate rule below).
@ref Kinnim 3:1-3:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:2-6 src:mishnah-kinnim-3:8-13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      what   IS A `What the priest did`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` counts what MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `offered all above` THEN JUST (sum counts)
    WHEN `offered all below` THEN JUST (sum counts)
    WHEN `offered half above and half below` THEN
        IF `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` counts
            THEN JUST (sum counts)
            ELSE JUST (2 TIMES (`the smallest majority of the nests` counts))
    WHEN `offered some other number above` THEN NOTHING

-- The same question under each reading of "the majority" (fork F3), when the priest offered half
-- above and half below.  NOTHING where a reading does not speak to the mixture.
@ref Kinnim 3:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:11-13)
GIVEN counts  IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      reading IS A `Reading of the majority`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fewest offerings certainly valid, half above and half below, under the reading` counts reading MEANS
    CONSIDER `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` counts reading
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (2 TIMES n)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Beyond the text: the worst case for any number of birds above.  Ravad takes the general principle to
-- reach unequal splits; R. Zerahiah ha-Levi says they are outside the mishnah (Reiss n. 21); Beller
-- applies the principle's reason to one and two with four above (Higayon 5, p. 157).  Koppel's later
-- general solution for an arbitrary split is not stated in Reiss, who calls it "too convoluted" to read
-- into the mishnah (n. 29).  Not the text; asked separately in the seat, and labelled so.
@ref Kinnim 3:3, the worst case applied beyond the text (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:18)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      above  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fewest offerings certainly valid for any number above, beyond the text` counts above MEANS
    IF above AT LEAST 0 AND above AT MOST (2 TIMES (sum counts)) AND (FLOOR above) EQUALS above
        THEN JUST (`the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` (`nests mixed together` counts) above)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- How many pairs the owners must bring again between them: the birds not certainly valid, as pairs.
-- Bartenura on 3:1: "since these nests are two women's, they bring one nest jointly and stipulate
-- between them" ("יביאו קן אחד בשותפות ויתנו ביניהן"); Ravad likewise (Reiss n. 14).
@ref Kinnim 3:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:6), as Bartenura reads it (bartenura-kinnim-3.txt line 3)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      what   IS A `What the priest did`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the pairs the owners must bring again together` counts what MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` counts what
    WHEN JUST valid THEN JUST (((2 TIMES (sum counts)) MINUS valid) DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `3:3 and 3:4 designated birds, offered by a priest who did not ask`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:15 | חטאת לזו ועולה לזו:
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:16 | עשה כולן למעלן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:17 | כולן למטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:18 | חצין למעלן וחצין למטן, שתיהן פסול, שאני אומר, חטאת קריבה למעלן ועולה למטן.
-- A sin offering to this woman and a burnt offering to that: he made them all above: half valid and
-- half invalid; all below: half valid and half invalid; half above and half below: both invalid, for I
-- say the sin offering was offered above and the burnt offering below.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:20 | חטאת ועולה וסתומה ומפורשת:
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:21 | עשה כולן למעלן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:22 | כולן למטן, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:23 | חצין למעלן וחצין למטן, אין כשר אלא סתומה, והיא מתחלקת ביניהן.
-- A sin offering and a burnt offering, an unassigned nest and a designated nest: he made them all
-- above: half valid and half invalid; all below: half valid and half invalid; half above and half
-- below: only the unassigned nest is valid, and it is divided between them.
-- (Bartenura: two women, three nests: one nest split into a burnt offering for one and a sin offering
-- for the other, one left unassigned, one designated as to its offerings but not as to its owner.  In
-- the encoding's terms: two designated sin offerings, two designated burnt offerings, one unassigned
-- pair.)
@ref Kinnim 3:3-3:4 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:15-18 src:mishnah-kinnim-3:20-23)
GIVEN m    IS A `Mixture`
      what IS A `What the priest did`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` m what MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `offered all above` THEN JUST (`the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` m (`the birds in the mixture` m))
    WHEN `offered all below` THEN JUST (`the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` m 0)
    WHEN `offered half above and half below` THEN
        IF even (`the birds in the mixture` m)
            THEN JUST (`the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` m ((`the birds in the mixture` m) DIVIDED BY 2))
            ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `offered some other number above` THEN NOTHING

-- "And it is divided between them": the unassigned nest's two offerings count one for each woman
-- (Bartenura: since they bought it jointly, one is quit of her sin offering and the other of her burnt
-- offering).
@ref Kinnim 3:4 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:23)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the unassigned nest counts one offering for each of the two women` MEANS TRUE

§§ `3:5 a designated bird and an obligation already partly offered`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:25 | חטאת שנתערבה בחובה, אין כשר אלא מנין חטאת שבחובה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:26 | חובה שנים בחטאת, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:27 | וחטאת שנים בחובה, המנין שבחובה כשר.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:28 | וכן עולה שנתערבה בחובה, אין כשר אלא מנין עולות שבחובה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:29 | חובה שנים בעולה, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:30 | עולה שנים בחובה, המנין שבחובה כשר.
-- A sin offering mixed with an obligation: only as many as the sin offerings in the obligation are
-- valid.  An obligation twice the sin offering: half valid and half invalid.  A sin offering twice in
-- the obligation: the number in the obligation is valid.  So too a burnt offering ...
-- (Bartenura: two nests, one of whose offerings has already been made, leave three birds owing two of
-- one kind and one of the other; one designated bird falls among them.  The priest here asks first, as
-- in chapter 1; the count is chapter 1's.)
@ref Kinnim 3:5 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:25-30)
GIVEN `the designated bird is a`  IS AN `Offering`
      `sin offerings still owed`  IS A NUMBER
      `burnt offerings still owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `the designated bird is a` `sin offerings still owed` `burnt offerings still owed` MEANS
    `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` m
    WHERE
        m MEANS `Mixture` WITH
                    `designated sin offerings`   IS IF `the designated bird is a` EQUALS `sin offering` THEN 1 ELSE 0
                    `designated burnt offerings` IS IF `the designated bird is a` EQUALS `burnt offering` THEN 1 ELSE 0
                    `unassigned obligations`     IS LIST (`Unassigned obligation` WITH
                                                              `sin offerings owed`   IS `sin offerings still owed`
                                                              `burnt offerings owed` IS `burnt offerings still owed`)

§§ `3:6 the vow made for the birth of a son`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:32 | האשה שאמרה "הרי עלי קן כשאלד זכר", ילדה זכר, מביאה שתי קנים, אחת לנדרה ואחת לחובתה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:33 | נתנתם לכהן, והכהן צריך לעשות שלש פרידים מלמעלן ואחת מלמטן, לא עשה כן, אלא עשה שתים למעלן ושתים למטן ולא נמלך, צריכה להביא עוד פרידה אחת ויקריבנה למעלן.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:34 | ממין אחד.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:35 | משני מינין, תביא שתים.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:36 | פירשה נדרה, צריכה להביא עוד שלש פרידים. ממין אחד.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:37 | משני מינין, תביא ארבע.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:38 | קבעה נדרה, צריכה להביא עוד חמש פרידים. ממין אחד.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:39 | משני מינין, תביא שש.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:40 | נתנתם לכהן ואין ידוע מה נתנה, הלך הכהן ועשה ואין ידוע מה עשה, צריכה להביא עוד ארבע פרידים לנדרה, ושתים לחובתה, וחטאת אחת.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:41 | בן עזאי אומר, שתי חטאות.
-- A woman who said "a nest upon me when I bear a male", and bore a male, brings two nests, one for her
-- vow and one for her obligation.  She gave them to the priest, and the priest should make three birds
-- above and one below.  He did not, but made two above and two below and did not ask: she must bring
-- one more bird and offer it above, of one species; of two species, she brings two.  She specified
-- her vow: she must bring three more birds, of one species; of two species, four.  She fixed her vow:
-- she must bring five more birds, of one species; of two species, six.  She gave them to the priest and
-- it is not known what she gave, and the priest went and made them and it is not known what he made:
-- she must bring four more birds for her vow, two for her obligation, and one sin offering.  Ben Azzai
-- says: two sin offerings.
-- Bartenura: "specified her vow" -- she said which birds were for the vow; "fixed her vow" -- she
-- named its species when she vowed and does not remember which.  The text's numbers are encoded as it
-- gives them; how they follow from covering every possible shortfall is shown below for the first two
-- cases.
@ref Kinnim 3:6 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:32-41)
GIVEN known          IS A `What is known of her vow`
      `of two species` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as Ben Azzai says` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the more birds she must bring` known `of two species` `as Ben Azzai says` MEANS
    CONSIDER known
    WHEN `she did not say which birds were for her vow` THEN IF `of two species` THEN 2 ELSE 1
    WHEN `she said which birds were for her vow`        THEN IF `of two species` THEN 4 ELSE 3
    WHEN `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it`    THEN IF `of two species` THEN 6 ELSE 5
    WHEN `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did` THEN
        4 PLUS 2 PLUS (IF `as Ben Azzai says` THEN 2 ELSE 1)

-- What one possible way the priest offered the four birds leaves her short, by species and offering.
DECLARE `Shortfall` HAS
    `turtledove sin offerings`     IS A NUMBER
    `turtledove burnt offerings`   IS A NUMBER
    `young pigeon sin offerings`   IS A NUMBER
    `young pigeon burnt offerings` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN ts IS A NUMBER
      tb IS A NUMBER
      ps IS A NUMBER
      pb IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Shortfall`
`short by` ts tb ps pb MEANS
    `Shortfall` WITH
        `turtledove sin offerings`     IS ts
        `turtledove burnt offerings`   IS tb
        `young pigeon sin offerings`   IS ps
        `young pigeon burnt offerings` IS pb

-- THE COVER: she brings enough of each species and offering to make good whichever shortfall is the
-- true one -- for each of the four, the most any possible way could leave her short.  (A sin offering
-- brought for a doubt is offered and not eaten: Bartenura.)
@ref Kinnim 3:6 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:33-41), as Bartenura reads it (bartenura-kinnim-3.txt lines 18-25)
GIVEN shortfalls IS A LIST OF `Shortfall`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the birds that make good every possible shortfall` shortfalls MEANS
        `the most of` (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `turtledove sin offerings`) shortfalls)
    PLUS `the most of` (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `turtledove burnt offerings`) shortfalls)
    PLUS `the most of` (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `young pigeon sin offerings`) shortfalls)
    PLUS `the most of` (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `young pigeon burnt offerings`) shortfalls)

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most of` xs MEANS maximum1 0 xs

-- Bartenura's possible shortfalls for the first two cases.  Two above and two below, where three
-- should have been above (the vow's two burnt offerings and the obligation's) and one below (the
-- obligation's sin offering).  One species: turtledoves.  Two species: the vow's turtledoves and the
-- obligation's young pigeons, where she said which; where she did not, either nest may be either.
-- READING (Bartenura), not the text; the text's numbers are the tests.
@ref Kinnim 3:6 (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:33-37), as Bartenura reads it (bartenura-kinnim-3.txt lines 18-22)
GIVEN known          IS A `What is known of her vow`
      `of two species` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Shortfall`
`the possible shortfalls, as Bartenura counts them` known `of two species` MEANS
    CONSIDER known
    WHEN `she did not say which birds were for her vow` THEN
        -- Any two birds above are valid burnt offerings and one below is the sin offering: one burnt
        -- offering is missing, of either nest's species.
        IF `of two species`
            THEN LIST `short by` 0 1 0 0, `short by` 0 0 0 1
            ELSE LIST `short by` 0 1 0 0
    WHEN `she said which birds were for her vow` THEN
        -- Both vow birds above: the obligation's two are below, and its burnt offering is missing.
        -- Both obligation birds above: the vow's two burnt offerings and the obligation's sin offering
        -- are missing.  One of each above: one of the vow's burnt offerings is missing.
        IF `of two species`
            THEN LIST `short by` 0 0 0 1, `short by` 0 2 1 0, `short by` 0 1 0 0
            ELSE LIST `short by` 0 1 0 0, `short by` 1 2 0 0, `short by` 0 1 0 0
    WHEN `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did` THEN EMPTY

§§ `3:6 the sayings at the end`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:42 | אמר רבי יהושע, זה הוא שאמרו, כשהוא חי קולו אחד, וכשהוא מת קולו שבעה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:43 | כיצד קולו שבעה?
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:44 | שתי קרניו, שתי חצוצרות.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:45 | שתי שוקיו, שני חלילין.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:46 | עורו לתוף, מעיו לנבלים, בני מעיו לכינורות.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:47 | ויש אומרים, אף צמרו לתכלת.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:48 | רבי שמעון בן עקשיא אומר, זקני עם הארץ, כל זמן שמזקינין, דעתן מיטרפת עליהן, שנאמר (איוב יב) "מסיר שפה לנאמנים וטעם זקנים יקח".
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-3:49 | אבל זקני תורה אינן כן, אלא כל זמן שמזקינין, דעתן מתישבת עליהן, שנאמר (שם) "בישישים חכמה ואורך ימים תבונה".
-- Rabbi Yehoshua said: this is what they said: while it lives its voice is one, and when it is dead its
-- voice is seven (its horns, legs, skin, intestines; some say its wool too).  Rabbi Shimon ben Akashya
-- says: the elders of the unlearned grow more confused as they age; the elders of Torah grow more
-- settled.  INERT: no rule.  (Bartenura reads Rabbi Yehoshua's saying of this case: before, she owed one
-- nest for her vow and one for her obligation; now, not knowing, she owes many more.)
